(1)  297/   16D7E :                     
(1)  298/   16D7E :                     		; Each sub-object deletes itself when it detects that its
(1)  299/   16D7E :                     		; parent is going to delete itself. This mostly works, but
(1)  300/   16D7E :                     		; does cause the sub-object to linger for one frame longer
(1)  301/   16D7E :                     		; than it should, which is why rolling into a Caterkiller
(1)  302/   16D7E :                     		; at high speed causes Sonic to be hurt.
(1)  303/   16D7E :                     
(1)  304/   16D7E :                     		; Has the head been destroyed?
